	<section_number>17.1-232</section_number>
	<catch_line>What to be recorded in judgment docket</catch_line>
	<text>
		Abstracts of all judgments authorized or required by law to be docketed or recorded shall be recorded in a book to be known as the judgment docket.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1919, § 3393, § 17-64; 1920, p. 314; 1932, p. 334; 1998, c. 872; 2002, c. 832.</history>
